              DIGITAL RELEASES FULL DCE CORE SERVICES
               FOR OpenVMS ALPHA AXP AND VAX SYSTEMS


  ... Extending its leadership in open client/server computing ...


MAYNARD, Mass. -- June 30, 1994 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
today announced that it has begun shipping DCE Security Server and 
DCE Cell Directory Server for OpenVMS V1.2. DCE provides a common 
set of support services for distributed applications in a 
multivendor environment.

     "This development makes the OpenVMS environment the first 
major non-UNIX server operating system to deliver full DCE core 
services. It is a testimony to Digital's strong commitment to 
provide customers with next-generation open software for the 
OpenVMS Alpha AXP and VAX platforms. Delivery of full DCE core 
services enables customers to build distributed applications that 
fully exploit the combined strengths of DCE and OpenVMS," claimed 
Jesse Lipcon, vice president, OpenVMS Systems Business Unit.  

     With full DCE core functionality now added to the extensive 
suite of open software already available for OpenVMS systems, 
customers and independent software vendors (ISVs) can build  
large-scale, multivendor applications, with increased confidence 
in a common set of vendor-neutral support services. The OpenVMS 
environment provides the system reliability, availability, security, 
and capacity needed in mission-critical applications. Furthermore, 
to encourage large-scale DCE implementations, Digital bundles the 
runtime services license with OpenVMS free of charge.

     DCE for OpenVMS supports an open computing environment where 
networks of multivendor systems appear to the user as a single 
system.  Since DCE makes the underlying networks and operating 
systems transparent, application developers can easily build 
portable, interoperable applications.  Users can locate and share 
information safely and easily across a multivendor enterprise, 
supported by a consistent model for naming and security.

     Digital is a leader in providing users the benefits of DCE 
technology. For example, Digital provided four of the seven DCE 
technologies to the Open Software Foundation (OSF). Digital has 
delivered full DCE functionality on DEC OSF/1 UNIX based platforms 
and now for OpenVMS, on both the VAX and Alpha AXP platforms. 
Future plans include DCE client versions for DOS/Windows and
Windows NT and an NT DCE server version. Also, Digital will be 
using DCE in key middleware products, such as ObjectBroker.

     Digital's proven expertise in distributed computing enables 
Digital to provide today a full suite of DCE Consulting and 
Integration Services. In recognition of the significant learning 
curve most customers face as they design and build new 
client/server infrastructures, Digital provides DCE support ranging
from a complete educational curriculum to onsite engineering 
development of a mission-critical application.

     "DCE is fast becoming the de facto standard for open 
client/server computing as more and more vendors ship DCE 
technology. We believe the DCE technology is a logical step for 
companies who want to tie together many platforms and operating 
system environments - the world is going to DCE," noted Jack 
Berger, president of Intraco Systems. "The bottom line is that we 
believe OpenVMS offers our customers an optimal operating system 
for a server and it is the most secure operating environment. The 
tremendous value of the DCE technology is that it allows businesses 
to plug into systems all over the universe; however, this advantage 
also opens up system security issues and concerns. But with 
OpenVMS, the security is already tightly embedded and it simply is 
not an issue!"

PRICING:

     DCE Application Development Kit license is $549.00

     DCE Runtime Services is licensed with the OpenVMS operating 
     system - Free

     DCE Cell Directory Server license is $2,195.00 *

     DCE Security Server license is $2,195.00 *

* Prices are for software licenses at U.S. List

AVAILABILITY:  Immediately.
 
     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems.  Digital's scalable Alpha AXP 
platforms, storage, networking, software and services, together 
with industry-focused solutions from business partners, help 
organizations compete and win in today's global marketplace. 
