                DIGITAL AND TechGnosis INK AGREEMENT
                 TO JOINTLY DEVELOP AND DISTRIBUTE
                     DATA INTEGRATION PRODUCTS


       ...Pact covers DB Integrator and SequeLink Middleware


MAYNARD, Mass. -- June 30, 1994 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
and TechGnosis International Incorporated announced today a 
worldwide development and distribution agreement for their 
multi-database management and data integration software products.

     Under the pact, Digital will offer the full suite of 
TechGnosis multiplatform ODBC-compliant SequeLink database server 
links and network transports, and TechGnosis will resell Digital's 
Database Integrator (DBI) multi-database management product and the 
DBI connections to RMS, DBMS, and DSM (MUMPS) databases. 

     According to Digital and TechGnosis, this agreement will 
expand customers' options for heterogeneous database integration.  
In addition to the numerous databases currently integrated through 
Digital's DBI product, including Rdb, Oracle, Sybase and DB2, the 
addition of SequeLink server links and network transports will 
expand management capabilities to AS/400, Informix, Ingres and
Adabas databases, as well. 

     "Our global customers look to Digital's software frameworks to 
help them make effective use of all their data independent of 
network, database system or location.  This relationship between 
two leaders in data integration strengthens our ability to deliver 
these capabilities to our customers," said Rose Ann Giordano, 
Digital's vice president for production systems software. "With 
SequeLink and DB Integrator, we will be able to offer high 
performance, cost effective access to dozens of DBMS's on virtually 
every hardware platform."

     "This alliance with Digital brings two product sets together 
that truly enhance one another," commented William F. Sullivan, COO 
of TechGnosis.  "Digital's DBI technology is extremely advanced.  
Together, we leverage the strength of the DBI technology with open 
access to the key data sources in the market using a single, 
logical data pipe. 

     This 'single pipe' means DBI can now talk to, for example, 
three different databases without requiring each vendor's database 
'net' product.  SequeLink greatly expands the number of supported 
database environments for DBI while DBI provides SequeLink users 
new, sophisticated cross platform capabilities," he continued. 

     SequeLink has been an industry-leading client/server 
middleware product for nearly a decade, and was originally 
developed for Digital systems.  It provided the first client/server 
access from desktops to relational databases, and today is 
available on virtually every hardware/software combination in the 
market. 

     Digital Equipment Corporation, with headquarters in Maynard, 
Massachusetts, is the world's leader in open client/server 
solutions from personal computing to integrated worldwide 
information systems.  Digital's scalable Alpha AXP platforms,
storage, networking, software and services, together with 
industry-focused solutions from business partners, help 
organizations compete and win in today's global marketplace. 

     Founded in 1987, TechGnosis is a privately held company with 
headquarters in Burlington, Massachusetts and is the market leader 
in Client/Server MiddleWare for heterogeneous environments with 
more than 4000 server installations worldwide.  TechGnosis 
maintains operations in the USA, Belgium, Japan, the United 
Kingdom, and Germany and has additional distribution of its 
products through its worldwide distributor, OEM, and value-added 
reseller partners. 
