      ORACLE AND DIGITAL ANNOUNCE ENTERPRISE SOLUTIONS PROGRAM


           ...Open Systems with Single Vendor Service...


MAYNARD, Mass. -- July 6, 1994 -- Oracle Corporation and Digital 
Equipment Corporation today announced the launch of the multi-
million dollar Enterprise Solutions Program (ESP).  This worldwide 
initiative will offer a complete suite of products and services to 
customers seeking mainframe alternatives. 

     With this initiative in place, Oracle and Digital will enable 
customers to obtain their products, consulting services, and 
support through a single contact.  Previously, customers seeking to 
migrate applications from mainframes to open systems needed to 
purchase the necessary products and services from multiple vendors.  
Therefore, due to the lack of a single source, customers did not 
receive the comprehensive level of support and services required. 

     "This initiative will enable mainframe customers to take 
advantage of the latest and most advanced systems and database 
technologies while maintaining the high level of support and 
service to which they are accustomed," said Beatriz Infante, vice 
president Digital Products Division, Oracle Corporation. 
"Oracle and Digital historically have had the most robust cluster 
offering on the market with the OpenVMS product lines.  We are 
bringing the same level of superior technology to our UNIX cluster 
offering," said Infante. 

Cost-Effective Access To Decision Critical Information

     Initially, customers seeking flexible access to decision 
support data will benefit most from this initiative. Oracle and 
Digital do not intend to replace the mainframe, but rather to 
provide better solutions for decision support applications that can 
benefit from moving to an open relational database environment. In 
the quarters ahead, Oracle and Digital will extend the initiative 
to include high volume transaction processing applications as well. 

     "Businesses need immediate access to decision critical 
information to remain competitive in a fast- paced global market.  
Oracle and Digital can enable businesses to have that access today 
so they can gain a competitive edge by moving quickly, efficiently, 
and intelligently," said Infante.  "In fact, successes we have had 
with customers in this area have fueled the formalization of this 
program," said Infante. 

Meeting Business Challenges With Joint Solutions

     Oracle and Digital will deliver products and services through 
joint technology, mission critical support, a rightsizing 
consulting practice, and a focused education and training program 
for Oracle and Digital sales personnel. 

Technology Alliance

     Oracle and Digital will deliver joint technology in four major 
areas:  Interoperability, Performance, Very Large Database (VLDB) 
support and High Availability.  "Both Digital and Oracle are known 
for excelling in the areas of research and engineering," stated 
William Strecker, vice president of Engineering and Chief Technical 
Officer of Digital Equipment Corporation.  "By combining our 
engineering talents into a joint development center for the 
Enterprise Solutions Program, we will enable the development and 
delivery of premier solutions." 

     The cornerstone technology of this program is Oracle and 
Digital's support for UNIX and OpenVMS technology.  Oracle and 
Digital jointly announce the availability of the following key 
technology components. 

     o 	UNIX Cluster Technology & Oracle Parallel Server -- As the 
        pioneers of clustered systems, Oracle and Digital lead the 
        way again with the Advantage Cluster Database Server. 
        Oracle's Parallel Server technology is highly optimized for 
        Digital's cluster technology due to aggressive joint 
        development and testing.  Running the Oracle Parallel 
        Server on Digital clusters, customers can take advantage of 
        failover capabilities for high availability. 

     o 	Memory Channel Cluster Interconnect -- Digital's 
        AdvantageCluster Database servers will feature Memory 
        Channel, a high bandwidth, high performance cluster 
        interconnect that offers up to 100 times the data carrying 
        capacity of conventional interconnects.  Memory Channel 
        interconnect, combined with Oracle's exceptional scaling on 
        Digital's SMP systems provides customers with uniquely
     	powerful solutions for business needs. 

     o 	Oracle7 Release 7.1 Parallel Query -- The Parallel Query 
        capabilities of Release 7.1 automatically decompose SQL 
        queries into tasks that are executed in multiple threads or 
        processes across parallel processors.  In Digital's UNIX
     	cluster environment, Parallel Query over Memory Channel 
        will execute a query across nodes of a cluster. 

     o 	Oracle Backup/Restore for POLYCENTER NetWorker Save and 
        Restore -- Backing up and restoring very large databases 
        quickly and efficiently is a requirement for mission 
        critical environments. Integrated with POLYCENTER NetWorker 
        Save and Restore, Oracle Backup/Restore can backup more 
        than 50GB per hour. 

     o 	Server Manager for POLYCENTER Manager on NetView -- This 
        new product integrates Oracle7 Release 7. l's Server 
        Manager and Network Manager with Digital's POLYCENTER 
        Manager on NetView, a comprehensive system management
     	solution for multivendor environments.  This new product 
        allows the entire distributed system to be managed from a 
        single console. 

     o 	ESP Connectivity Products -- Oracle and Digital enable 
        customers to have complex distributed database systems by 
        providing all the products customers need to set up an 
        integrated, heterogeneous, manageable distributed
     	environment. 

     o 	ESP Development Center -- To meet additional core 
        technology requirements for this program, Oracle and 
        Digital have established an ESP Development Center located 
        in Redwood Shores, CA, and staffed by Oracle and Digital 
        engineers. 

     "Calendar year 1994 will prove that Digital's UNIX cluster 
running the Oracle Parallel Server is far ahead of any competitor's 
solution," said John O'Keefe, vice president, UNIX Systems 
Marketing, Digital Equipment Corporation.  "Customers will also 
benefit from Oracle's and Digital's data integration and 
connectivity products and services from both companies which will 
enable them to maintain heterogeneous information systems 
environments and preserve their investments in legacy systems," 
said O'Keefe. 

Support, Consulting, Sales and Marketing Alliance

     As part of ESP, Oracle and Digital intend to announce 
alliances in the areas of premium support for customers with 
mission critical environments, rightsizing consulting, and sales 
and marketing. These Alliances will focus on both DEC OSF/I and 
OpenVMS operating system environments.  Look for follow up 
announcements throughout 1994. 

Availability

     Oracle and Digital will begin the rollout of this program with 
a small set of key customers in the second half of calendar year 
1994 and deliver products and services to the general market in 
1995. 

     Oracle Corporation, a $2 billion company with headquarters in 
Redwood Shores, Calif., is the world's leading supplier of 
information management software. Oracle develops and markets the 
Oracle7 family of software products for database management; 
Cooperative Development Environment (CDE), a complete set of CASE
and application development tools for enterprise-wide, client/
server computing; and Oracle Applications, packaged client/server 
solutions for human resources, accounting and manufacturing.  
Oracle software runs on personal digital assistants, PCs, 
workstations, minicomputers, mainframes and massively parallel
computers.  The company offers its products, along with related 
consulting, education and support services, in over 90 countries 
around the world. 

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems. Digital's scalable Alpha AXP 
platforms, storage, networking, software and services, together 
with industry-focused solutions from business partners, help 
organizations compete and win in today's global marketplace. 
