MAYNARD, Mass. -- July 19, 1994 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
today announced the promotion of Raymond L. Weadock to vice 
president and general manager, the Americas area, of the company's 
Personal Computer Business Unit, effective immediately.

     In his new role, Weadock, 41, will be responsible for all 
aspects of PC product sales and marketing for the Americas. Weadock 
will report directly to Bernhard Auer, worldwide vice president and 
general manager, Digital's Personal Computer Business Unit, which 
is headquartered in Acton, Mass.

     "Ray Weadock brings extensive experience in sales, operations 
and business management, with a strong emphasis on developing 
channels relationships," Auer commented. "Ray's experience makes 
him an excellent choice to help move Digital's Personal Computer 
Business Unit into its second phase of market expansion," he added. 

     Weadock previously was vice president of sales, Americas area, 
for the Personal Computer Business Unit, which included direct 
sales, catalog sales, and indirect channel sales and marketing. 
Prior to joining Digital in February, Weadock was vice president of 
the worldwide distribution products group for Conner Peripherals 
Corporation, where he also served as vice president of America's 
distribution sales. Previously, he was vice president and chief 
operating officer of Plus Corporation, which later merged with 
Quantum Corporation. Prior to that role, Weadock served as a 
director of worldwide sales for Visicorp Corporation.

     Weadock is a graduate of the Executive Institute at Stanford 
University's Graduate School of Business and holds a bachelor of 
science degree in business administration from the University of 
Arkansas.

