          DIGITAL EQUIPMENT ANNOUNCES NEW HIGH-PERFORMANCE
                STORAGE ARRAYS AND BACKUP SUBSYSTEMS
                    FOR NOVELL NETWARE NETWORKS


     StorageWorks RAID Array 210 and DLT Single- and Multiple-
        Cartridge Subsystems Offer Industry's Most Flexible,
                     Scalable Storage Solutions


MAYNARD, Mass. -- July 25, 1994 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
today expanded its portfolio of storage solutions for PC networks with
a range of new modular, scalable disk and tape storage subsystems
designed for industry-standard, Intel-based hardware running Novell
NetWare, v. 3.1X and 4.0X.

     The StorageWorks RAID Array 210, a controller-based disk array, is
a competitively priced Novell RAID solution offering extended fault
tolerance -- with redundant disks, power supplies, cooling fans and
error-detection and recovery software. The RAID Array 210, Digital's
second-generation RAID solution for NetWare, ensures continuous access
to critical applications and provides complete data protection. In a
standard configuration, the product comes equipped with three 1.05GB or
2.1GB disks with room for three additional disks in the same enclosure.

The StorageWorks TZ87N family of digital linear tape (DLT) subsystems
for NetWare provides the industry's fastest and most robust tape backup
and hierarchical storage management (HSM) storage options, and is
available in two configurations to match various user needs. The
single-cartridge TZ87N offers up to 10GB (20GB compressed) of storage
capacity, while the five cartridge autoloader subsystem provides up to
50GB (100GB compressed) of capacity. Both products offer the
reliability required for continuous high-duty cycle usage at speeds
two-to-three times faster than conventional 4mm and 8mm tape systems.
In a separate announcement today, Cheyenne Software announced that its
ARCserve 5.01d backup software for NetWare fully supports Digital's
TZ87N family (see news release from Cheyenne Software for more
information).

     According to Robert Rennick, vice president of Digital's Storage
Subsystems business, "Many IS departments are rapidly downsizing their
information systems, sparking a growing need for dependable and
manageable mission-critical storage products on client/server
architectures. Others are 'upsizing' for the first time, from
stand-alone PCs, or simple peer-to-peer networks, to client/server
networks. With our expanded StorageWorks RAID and DLT families for PC
networks, Digital now meets the needs of both user categories with
products that offer unmatched performance, reliability and
price-performance leadership."

     "With their ease-of-installation and use, and inherent 
flexibility, StorageWorks offers the benefits of dedicated storage 
subsystems to a range of Novell users," added Bruce Baird, segment 
marketing manager of Digital's StorageWorks for PC networks. "The new
RAID Array 210 and TZ87N DLT family provide fast performance, are
highly reliable, and require virtually no maintenance. Furthermore,
because the StorageWorks architecture is based on a building-block
approach, we are unique in our ability to provide affordability as
users' needs and applications grow."

StorageWorks RAID Array 210 -- Fault Tolerance, Flexible Configurations

     The StorageWorks RAID Array 210 for NetWare provides reliable, 
expandable, cost-effective storage for every level of RAID performance. 
With a 4MB FastCache (expandable to 32MB), the RAID Array 210 is
optimized for fast read-write operations. Other product features
include:

Ease-of-use and Reliability

     -	Easy installation, maintenance and expansion with 
        "plug-'n-go" architecture and snap-in components

     -	Extended fault tolerance through redundant disk drives, 
        power supplies, and cooling fans

     -	Continuous access to data via automatic, unattended 
        rebuilds and hot spare/hot swap disk drive configurations

     -	Lower costs and improved reliability with a single board 
        solution combining an EISA to SCSI adapter and RAID 
        controller

Flexibility

     -	Building-block architecture for easy, cost-effective 
        expansion

     -	Platform independence via open storage solutions

     -	Modular and scalable disk drive configurations -- up to 7 
        drives per single-channel controller, and 21 drives per 
        three-channel controller

     -	Full support of RAID 0, 1, 0+1, 5 or JBOD (Just a Bunch of 
        Disks)

     -	Supports multiple RAID levels within the same disk array

StorageWorks TZ87N DLT -- High Capacity, Fast Performance, High Reliability

     The StorageWorks TZ87N family of DLT subsystems offers the fastest
and highest capacity tape drives available, industry leading data
integrity, and a range of leading third-party software support,
including products from Palindrome Corporation, and now Cheyenne
Software. With DLTs advanced linear tape path design, the TZ87N offers
superior performance and outstanding reliability. The TZ87N comes in a
range of configurations, including a StorageWorks 5.25-inch "building
block," a separate tabletop enclosure, and a 5-cartridge tabletop
loader subsystem. The wide choice of capacities and enclosures allows
for maximum configuration flexibility. In addition, the TZ87N offers:

     -	Unattended high performance backup -- up to 150 MB per 
        minute, two-to-three-times faster than 4mm and 8mm drives

     -	Industry leading capacity -- up to twice as much storage 
        space as 4mm and 8mm drives

     -	Reliable operation for maximum data availability in 
        high-duty cycle tape applications such as HSM -- five times 
        the estimated drive-life of 8mm devices

     According to Matt Plociak, Executive Vice President of NETLAN Inc,
"Our customers are increasingly seeking a complement of on-line and
near-line storage solutions in affordable, modular form factors for
their client/server networks. Digital's newest StorageWorks for Novell
products are uniquely suited to provide these capabilities. Many of
our customers will 'discover' RAID and DLT because of StorageWorks."

     StorageWorks is a comprehensive family of disk, tape and optical
storage subsystems, offering modular, competitively-priced, 
industry-standard solutions in customizable desktop, deskside and 
datacenter enclosures. StorageWorks products are available on multiple
operating systems and hardware platforms, including Novell 
environments, Sun Microsystems workstations, and Digital workstations
and midrange computers.

Pricing and Availability

     The StorageWorks RAID Array 210 Subsystem is priced at $6,999 for
a base configuration, and consists of a StorageWorks hardware 
controller, RAID software, and a deskside pedestal enclosure with three
1.05GB disk drives, redundant power supplies and fans, and room for
three additional disk drives. The StorageWorks TZ87N DLT tape drive
building block and tabletop enclosure are each priced at $4,999, and
the 5-cartridge DLT autoloader subsystem is priced at $9,999. All
products are now available from select value-added resellers (VARs),
wholesale distributors and systems integrators.  Call 1-800-STORWORKS
for more information.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated worldwide
information systems. Digital's scalable Alpha AXP platforms, storage,
networking, software and services, together with industry-focused
solutions from business partners, help organizations compete and win in
today's global marketplace.
