         ALPHA AXP PLATFORM DELIVERS BETTER-THAN-REAL-TIME
            PERFORMANCE FOR ADVANCED ETMSP SIMULATIONS
       

SAN FRANCISCO, CA -- July 25, 1994 -- Digital Equipment Corporation's 
DEC 3000 Model 500X Alpha AXP system has provided better-than-real-time 
performance for a valuable new tool used to determine the stability of 
large, interconnected power systems. The Extended Transient/Midterm 
Stability Program (ETMSP), developed by a team from Powertech Labs, 
Inc. under the sponsorship of the Electric Power Research Institute 
(EPRI) of Palo Alto, CA, is a time-domain simulation program for 
non-linear analyses based on stepwise numerical integration. ETMSP 
simulates very large systems and incorporates efficient numerical 
methods, including the implicit trapezoidal rule, to attain maximum 
solution speed. The program's advanced capabilities and performance 
are on display here this week in Powertech's demonstration suite at 
the 1994 IEEE conference. 

     "ETMSP is designed to run on a number of platforms," said Dr.
Prabha Kundur, Vice President, Powertech Labs, Inc. "However, only
the Alpha AXP machine was able to run the program at such an
impressive level of performance for a typically sized system model
with 1023 buses and 115 generators modeled in detail."

     ETMSP includes all modeling capabilities required for 
simulation of time extending beyond the typical transient timeframe
into the midterm time period in which devices such as transformer
under-load tap changers and generator field current limiters are
active. As a result, the program is ideal for transient stability
analysis as well as voltage stability assessment where simulations
of several minutes are often required. ETMSP also incorporates
enhanced modeling of FACTS devices, HVdc, ULTCs, field current
limiters, and turbine and speed governing systems. Sophisticated,
user-defined modeling capabilities complete the program's
comprehensive features.

     "ETMSP gives engineers unprecedented capabilities for 
performing a wide range of essential planning and operating 
studies," said Terry Ray, worldwide director of Digital's Utilities
Industry Segment. "Alpha AXP technology allows them to achieve
better-than-real-time performance, thereby creating a comprehensive
and powerful solution for managing large, interconnected power
systems. In addition, the algorithms, portability, and speed of
the Alpha AXP system make ETMSP ideal for many research
applications."  

     Using ETMSP, engineers can now complete a wide variety of 
studies more efficiently and accurately. For example, the 
determination of transient stability limits involving repetitive 
simulations of relatively short lengths can be performed very 
rapidly with the program, allowing limits to be quickly located. 
The study of inter-area oscillations generally requires lengthy 
simulations using models of very large systems which may involve 
excessive CPU times when conventional simulation tools are used. 
ETMSP reduces the time needed for such simulations, leaving more 
time for results analysis. The program also makes it much easier 
to find voltage stability limits and assess the impacts of load 
shedding or capacitor switching on the limits, as well as to 
perform detailed studies on the impact and performance of FACTS 
devices and special control systems.

     ETMSP is one of a series of programs which comprise EPRI's 
advanced Power Systems Analysis Package (PSAPAC) for power industry
use. Other programs include LOADSYN for load model synthesis,
DYNRED for dynamic reduction, VSTAB for the analysis of voltage
stability, SSSP for small signal stability, LTSP for long-term
stability, and IPFLOW for powerflow analysis. The outstanding
performance of ETMSP in its evaluation phase has led EPRI to launch
a project (RP3103-7) which will result in the migration of the
technology to an on-line environment in which the program will be
used as an engine for dynamic security assessment.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems. Digital's scalable Alpha AXP 
platforms, storage, networking, software and services, together 
with industry-focused solutions from business partners, help 
organizations compete and win in today's global marketplace.
