           DIGITAL AND MEGATEK TO PURSUE HIGH PERFORMANCE
                       3D GRAPHICS SOLUTIONS


ORLANDO, FL -- July 26, 1994 -- ACM '94 SIGGRAPH Conference --
Digital Equipment Corporation of Maynard, MA and MEGATEK
Corporation of San Diego announced today that the two companies
have agreed to work together for the purpose of developing
high-performance 3D graphics solutions. The relationship will
combine the strengths of Digital's Alpha AXP 64-bit RISC
architecture workstation family with MEGATEK's proprietary
INSTACUITY (tm) Visual Enhancement graphics technology.

     "The goal of this agreement is to provide a very
high-performance, high-quality 3D system that will increase 
productivity for design engineers by featuring a broad spectrum
of advanced rendering capabilities," said Willy Shih, Vice
President, UNIX/Windows NT Systems for Digital. "Megatek has a
long track record for providing graphics technology to meet the
needs of users running demanding design applications. We expect
to satisfy those needs with the technology we are developing
together."

     "The Alpha AXP family of workstations continues to gain
industry-wide acceptance and extraordinary popularity because of
its outstanding compute performance," said Robert Benders,
MEGATEK President. "Its wide bandwidth architecture is ideally 
suited to match the formidable demands required for ultra-high 
performance graphics."

     The initial plans included in the agreement call for 
development of technologies to produce advanced rendering solutions
previously available only from companies having special-purpose,
high-cost systems.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated
worldwide information systems. Digital's scalable Alpha AXP
platforms, storage, networking, software and services, together
with industry-focused solutions from business partners, help
organizations compete and win in today's global marketplace.

     MEGATEK Corporation, a Nihon Unisys company, is an OEM 
supplier of graphics accelerators for open system workstation
applications that include standard UNIX (R), the X Window System
(tm), PEX and PHIGS software.
