Orlando, FL -- July 26, 1994 -- ACM '94 SIGGRAPH Conference, 
Booth 1006-- Digital Equipment Corporation of Maynard, MA was a
major presence at the opening today of the premier conference and
exhibition for graphics and multimedia users. The exhibit includes
demonstrations of Digital's extensive array of applications
including video and sound creation and editing, video
telecollaboration, and audio/video mail, along with workstations
and systems delivering the applications.
 
Performance leading workstations and graphics
 
     Technologies include Digital's newly announced DEC 3000 Model 
700 AXP and Model 900 AXP workstations, the fastest on the desktop
and the fastest in the world respectively, along with new graphics
accelerators. These new graphics accelerators, the ZLX-E models 2
and 3, provide customers with the highest 2D performance and the
highest 3D wireframe performance on the desktop of any workstations
in the industry. Both also give customers the the best
price/performance.
 
     The DEC 3000 Model 700 AXP workstation is based on the DECchip
21064A, a new microprocessor in the Alpha AXP family running at 225
MHz. In both integer and floating point performance, the new unit
exceeds that of any other desktop system available. The companion
DEC 3000 Model 900 AXP workstation is built around a 275 MHz
version of the DECchip 21064A microprocessor, and provides
performance exceeding any other workstation on the market.
Digital's full line of Alpha AXP workstations can use the new
members of the ZLX-E family of graphics accelerators which provide
high levels of 2D and 3D performance at very competitive prices.
The new workstations and graphics options are described in the 
accompanying press release.
 
     Among the products shown in the Digital exhibit are designed 
to speed and simplify the development of multimedia applications.
These include Open3D, Digital's standards-based programming
interfaces for graphics; VPE (Visual Programming Environment) from
VPE; VideoEA and MediaEA from EnerAnalytics, TicTacToon superior
cartoon animation tools from 2001, and Multimedia Services for DEC 
OSF/1.
 
     Digital offers developers a comprehensive suite of tools which
allow development and deployment of applications for the most
demanding customer requirements which are built around the Alpha
AXP architecture.
 
Options and systems provide new capabilities for applications
 
     Alpha AXP systems can be equipped with a variety of options to
meet the needs of demanding multimedia and graphics users. The
Sound and Motion J300 audio and video adapter provides for high
quality audio and video recording and playback. DECtalk software
provides the text-to-speech technology which leads the industry.
Carrera Computers Cobra family offers a desktop workstation based
on the Alpha AXP technology which is well suited to multimedia and
animation applications. Digital's Velocitor disk drive subsystems
are the world's fastest and deliver data at the speeds needed for
real-time animation and graphics.
 
     The Digital 2100 A500MP server, announced last Spring, offers 
users outstanding performance and price/performance in a small
pedestal package which can be expanded from one to four Alpha AXP
processors and include up to 2 Gbyte of memory and 28 Gbyte of disk
storage in the space of a file cabinet.
 
     Digital's MFX600, a Multi-headed X-Terminal, supports live 
video and can be configured as separate screens, one virtual screen
or combinations, and can support up to six display monitors.
 
Applications for more efficiency
 
     Applications which can be deployed today and which take 
advantage of the advanced features of Digital's Alpha AXP systems
family include:
 
    o  Soundtrack Express and Melody Maker from Blue Ribbon 
       Soundworks
    
    o  VOXEL-MAN - 3D solid model medical imaging
    
    o  AVS - Scientific visualization of complex data
    
    o  Pro/ENGINEER - Mechanical design on the world's fastest 
       desktop
    
    o  Visual Reality - Tools for model, editing, and rendering 
       running on Windows NT
    
    o  Communique!- Multi-vendor, multi-point desktop video 
       conferencing with collaborative tools.
    
